{"id":"1fb82a13435777f321b9d0d6cbc7d259e19fdf32","axis":"silent","repo":"openvinotoolkit/openvino","sha":"1fb82a13435777f321b9d0d6cbc7d259e19fdf32","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"src/frontends/gguf/docs/mmproj.md","lines":["@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ audio branch. Built-in entries come from `projector_catalog` in"," | Vision | `gemma3nv` | MobileNet stem, UIR, attention and multiscale feature branches; vision-only support |"," | Vision | `minicpmv4_6` | window attention, two-stage merging |"," | Vision | `minicpmv4_7` | window-attention and direct 2x2 merging; packed-patch GenAI layout |","+| Vision | `minicpm_ocr_1_0` | MiniCPM-V 4.6 encoder graph; direct 2x2 merging in the published `-4x` projector |"," | Vision | `qwen2vl_merger`, `qwen2.5vl_merger`, `qwen3vl_merger` | temporal pairs, M-RoPE, windows (2.5), DeepStack (3) |"," | Vision | `pixtral` | 2D RoPE, patch merger, row separators |"," | Vision | `phi4` | dynamic resolution, resized positions |","@@ -48,7 +49,7 @@ The LFM2.5 vocoder is a separate `lfm2.audio_vocoder` architecture."," Not implemented: `ldp`, `ldpv2`, `adapter`, `step3vl`, `llama4`,"," `kimivl`, `paddleocr`, `lightonocr`, `cogvlm`, `dots_ocr`, `glm4v`, `youtuvl`, `yasa2`,"," `kimik25`, `nemotron_v2_vl`, `exaone4_5`, `hunyuanvl`, `granite_speech`, `mimovl`,","-`granite4_vision`. An unsupported projector fails conversion of the whole file.","+`granite4_vision`, `cohere2v`. An unsupported projector fails conversion of the whole file."," "," ## Validation coverage"," ","@@ -59,6 +60,11 @@ Not implemented: `ldp`, `ldpv2`, `adapter`, `step3vl`, `llama4`,","   [nightly](../../../../tests/model_hub_tests/gguf/gguf_mmproj_nightly) lists run real","   checkpoints with generated inputs. Per-checkpoint relaxations and skips are recorded in those","   lists.","+- `minicpm_ocr_1_0` needs llama.cpp `604cc43` or later. The model-hub oracle is pinned to an","+  older revision, so this projector is not in the model-hub lists. MiniCPM-OCR-1.0","+  `mmproj-model-f16-4x.gguf` (revision `0133ad8d`) was checked manually against","+  `mmproj_oracle` at `604cc43` on CPU with f32 inference precision at 448×448 and 280×420:","+  NMSE 8.1e-5 and 1.1e-4 on the BF16 file, 7.7e-7 and 6.7e-7 on its represented-F32 copy."," - Encoder tests do not validate media preprocessing, media insertion or complete VLM/audio","   generation. A catalog entry is not a claim of coverage for every checkpoint, resolution,","   quantization or device."],"additions":7,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/frontends/gguf/docs/supported_models.md","lines":["@@ -39,10 +39,10 @@ Tested models list real checkpoints and their quantization. `—` means no check"," | `hunyuan-dense` | Hunyuan-0.5B-Instruct Q8_0 | Learned QK-norm after RoPE |"," | `hunyuan-moe` | Hunyuan-A13B-Instruct Q2_K | QK-norm after RoPE, routed and shared experts |"," | `jais2` | Jais-2-8B-Chat Q4_K_M | Biased LayerNorm, ungated ReLU² FFN |","-| `lfm2` | LFM2-350M / LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct Q4_0 | LFM2 / LFM2.5 dense hybrid short convolution and GQA, QK-norm, tied head |","+| `lfm2` | LFM2-350M / LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct Q4_0; LFM2.5-Encoder-230M/350M, -Embedding-350M, -ColBERT-350M Q8_0 | LFM2 / LFM2.5 dense hybrid short convolution and GQA, QK-norm, tied head; noncausal encoders with pooling and `dense_2` projection |"," | `lfm2.audio_vocoder` | LFM2.5-Audio-1.5B Q4_0 ([audio components](mmproj.md#lfm2-audio-components)) | Standalone speech component; accepts the existing publisher architecture string |"," | `lfm2moe` | LFM2.5-8B-A1B Q4_0 | LFM2 / LFM2.5 MoE hybrid, dense lead, biased normalized expert routing |","-| `lfm3` | LFM3-1.7B / LFM3-VL-2B / LFM3-Audio-2B / LFM3-Omni-2B Q4_0 | Dense hybrid convolution/GQA, per-head output gates, paired optional post norms, tied output, mixed full/sliding RoPE |","+| `lfm3` | LFM3-1.7B / LFM3-VL-2B / LFM3-Audio-2B / LFM3-Omni-2B / D1-2B Q4_0 | Dense hybrid convolution/GQA, per-head output gates, paired optional post norms, tied output, mixed full/sliding RoPE; stateless D1 whole-prompt logits |"," | `llama` | Devstral Small 2507 24B Q4_K_M | llama-2 / llama-3, YaRN |"," | `llama-embed` | Llama-Nemotron-Embed-1B-v2 Q4_K_M | Per-token embeddings; mean/first/last pooling; causal or bidirectional |"," | `maincoder` | Maincoder-1B Q4_K_M | NORMAL RoPE, QK-norm after RoPE |","@@ -74,7 +74,10 @@ Tested models list real checkpoints and their quantization. `—` means no check","   `nemotron_h_moe` are not supported. See [runtime.md](runtime.md#stateful-and-genai-conversion)."," - **Multimodal:** a tested language backbone does not cover its vision or audio encoders,","   preprocessing or application pipeline.","-- **Model variants:** the `lfm3` builder supports causal autoregressive backbones; Decision/D1 variants are unsupported.","+- **Model variants:** the `lfm3` builder supports causal autoregressive backbones and stateless D1","+  (`lfm3.attention.causal=false`) whole-prompt logits; the LFM2 Decision head","+  (`lfm2.decision.block_count`) is unsupported. D1 has no GenAI adaptation; its iterative denoising","+  sampler is left to the application."," - **Quantization and memory:** see [quantization.md](quantization.md)."," "," ## llama.cpp cgraph path","@@ -114,8 +117,27 @@ codec components; the existing publisher architecture string is also accepted."," It consumes hidden states and codec codes rather than text tokens; see"," [audio component inputs and outputs](mmproj.md#lfm2-audio-components)."," ","-Noncausal LFM2 embedding/encoder/ColBERT variants need centered convolution and their","-embedding/pooling output contracts and are rejected explicitly. LFM2.5-Audio's `lfm2a`","+Noncausal LFM2.5 encoder, embedding and ColBERT checkpoints (`lfm2.attention.causal=false`)","+convert to stateless models with one `embeddings` output: centered short convolutions,","+bidirectional attention, then mean/CLS/last pooling (`lfm2.pooling_type`) and the optional","+`dense_2` projection, matching llama.cpp. Without pooling they return per-token rows, one model","+call per sequence; inputs are `inp_tokens` and `inp_pos` (positions `0..T-1`). Noncausal","+attention is accepted only for `lfm2`, not `lfm2moe`. Five F32 fixtures cover per-token, mean-with-biased-projection, CLS, last and","+ColBERT outputs. LFM3 D1 (`lfm3` with `lfm3.attention.causal=false`) reads a whole prompt with","+bidirectional full-attention layers and causal sliding-window layers. Its inputs are","+`inp_tokens`, `inp_pos`, `self_kq_mask_swa` and `inp_out_ids`; it returns logits for the rows","+selected by `inp_out_ids` (pass `0..T-1` for every token) and has no KV or convolution state.","+","+Real checkpoints were compared with llama.cpp `604cc430239c76ff636c443e3400bf552b750421` CPU on","+identical tokens. Q8_0 NMSE is `1.29e-4` for LFM2.5-ColBERT-350M, `3.12e-4` (CLS) for LFM2.5-Embedding-350M, `1.77e-3` for","+LFM2.5-Encoder-230M and `8.94e-4` for LFM2.5-Encoder-350M; the same weights represented in F32","+give `6.7e-8`, `2.3e-7`, `1.2e-6` and `4.4e-7`. D1-2B Q4_0 matches every top-1 token for six prompt","+positions with NMSE `3.0e-4..3.8e-3`, and `<1e-10` represented in F32. Revisions are","+`bc240003aba07253e261a8aaf0d2c9683318a967`, `a80de9c5b941d429104f0038292a0ef5a860e486`,","+`bb26e78c7164b386028928ebfcecebcc42467689`, `6559103d6c7136150cf989a4eda1462e5ef7b0c4` and","+`4a181094d1b6addfaa3a0956f78e7ab2aa406a0c` from LiquidAI's GGUF repositories.","+","+LFM2.5-Audio's `lfm2a`"," conformer projector and LFM2.5 speech components are supported as described in"," [mmproj.md](mmproj.md#lfm2-audio-components). GenAI waveform preprocessing and generation"," require the `gguf-frontend-mmproj` integration. Older Mimi-based LFM2 speech output"],"additions":27,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/frontends/gguf/src/builder/arch/lfm_builder.cpp","lines":["@@ -11,11 +11,29 @@"," "," namespace ov::frontend::gguf {"," namespace {","-DecoderParameters lfm_decoder_parameters(const GgufMetadata& metadata, bool lfm3) {","+// Noncausal LFM2 encoders and LFM3 D1 read a whole prompt in one stateless batch.","+void make_stateless(DecoderParameters& parameters) {","+    parameters.embedding_model = true;","+    parameters.model_contract.batchable_recurrent.reset();","+    parameters.model_contract.sequence_outputs.clear();","+    parameters.model_contract.supports_genai_adaptation = false;","+}","+","+DecoderParameters lfm_decoder_parameters(const GgufMetadata& metadata, const std::string& arch) {","+    const bool lfm3 = arch == \"lfm3\";","     if (!lfm3) {","         DecoderOptions options;","         options.normalize_expert_weights = true;","-        return resolve_decoder_parameters(metadata, RopeMode::Neox, options);","+        auto parameters = resolve_decoder_parameters(metadata, RopeMode::Neox, options);","+        if (!parameters.causal_attention) {","+            OPENVINO_ASSERT(arch == \"lfm2\", \"[GGUF] noncausal attention is supported only for lfm2, not \", arch);","+            OPENVINO_ASSERT(parameters.attention.window_size <= 0,","+                            \"[GGUF] noncausal LFM2 does not support sliding-window attention\");","+            OPENVINO_ASSERT(metadata.get_int(\"lfm2.decision.block_count\").value_or(0) == 0,","+                            \"[GGUF] LFM2 decision heads are not supported\");","+            make_stateless(parameters);","+        }","+        return parameters;","     }","     OPENVINO_ASSERT(metadata.has(\"lfm3.attention.sliding_window_pattern\") &&","                         metadata.has(\"lfm3.attention.sliding_window\") && metadata.has(\"lfm3.rope.freq_base_swa\"),","@@ -48,6 +66,10 @@ DecoderParameters lfm_decoder_parameters(const GgufMetadata& metadata, bool lfm3","                         \"[GGUF] LFM3 sliding-window flags must select attention layers\");","         parameters.layers[layer].recurrent = kv_heads[layer] == 0;","     }","+    if (!parameters.causal_attention) {","+        make_stateless(parameters);","+        parameters.pooling_type = 0;","+    }","     return parameters;"," }"," ","@@ -62,25 +84,34 @@ class LfmBuilder : public ModelBuilder {","                         \"[GGUF] \",","                         lfm3 ? \"LFM3\" : \"LFM2\",","                         \" requires shortconv.l_cache > 1\");","-        OPENVINO_ASSERT(g.metadata().get_bool(g.arch() + \".attention.causal\").value_or(true),","-                        lfm3 ? \"[GGUF] LFM3 decision models are not supported\"","-                             : \"[GGUF] noncausal LFM2 embedding models require a centered convolution builder\");","-        const auto parameters = lfm_decoder_parameters(g.metadata(), lfm3);","+        const auto parameters = lfm_decoder_parameters(g.metadata(), g.arch());","+        const bool causal = parameters.causal_attention;","+        // Noncausal LFM2 is a sentence or token encoder; noncausal LFM3 (D1) keeps its LM head.","+        const bool encoder = !causal && !lfm3;","         const auto dims = g.configure_decoder(parameters);","         OPENVINO_ASSERT(dims.layers > 0 && dims.embedding > 0,","                         \"[GGUF] LFM decoder requires positive layer and embedding counts\");","         auto weights = g.tensors();","-        const bool detokenizer = !lfm3 && weights.has(\"dense_2.weight\");","-        const auto output_weight = weights.require(detokenizer                    ? \"dense_2.weight\"","-                                                   : weights.has(\"output.weight\") ? \"output.weight\"","-                                                                                  : \"token_embd.weight\");","+        const bool detokenizer = causal && !lfm3 && weights.has(\"dense_2.weight\");","+        const auto output_weight = encoder                        ? weights(\"dense_2.weight\")","+                                   : detokenizer                  ? weights.require(\"dense_2.weight\")","+                                   : weights.has(\"output.weight\") ? weights.require(\"output.weight\")","+                                                                  : weights.require(\"token_embd.weight\");","         if (detokenizer)","             OPENVINO_ASSERT(output_weight.ne(0) == dims.embedding && output_weight.ne(1) == 1282,","                             \"[GGUF] LFM2 audio detokenizer requires a 1282-channel spectral head\");","         g.build_inp_pos();","-        g.build_attn_inp_kv();","+        if (causal)","+            g.build_attn_inp_kv();","+        else if (lfm3)","+            g.add_input(\"self_kq_mask_swa\", ov::element::f32, ov::PartialShape{1, 1, -1, -1});","         auto cur = g.build_inp_embd(weights.require(\"token_embd.weight\"));","-        const auto out_ids = detokenizer ? GgufValue{} : g.build_inp_out_ids();","+        const auto out_ids = detokenizer || encoder ? GgufValue{} : g.build_inp_out_ids();","+        const auto conv_padding = causal ? LfmConvPadding::STATE","+                                  : lfm3 ? LfmConvPadding::CAUSAL","+                                         : LfmConvPadding::CENTERED;","+        OPENVINO_ASSERT(conv_padding != LfmConvPadding::CENTERED || *kernel % 2 == 1,","+                        \"[GGUF] a centered short convolution requires an odd kernel\");","         for (int layer = 0; layer < dims.layers; ++layer) {","             const auto prefix = \"blk.\" + std::to_string(layer) + \".\";","             const auto weight = [&](const std::string& name) {","@@ -99,6 +130,9 @@ class LfmBuilder : public ModelBuilder {","                 const auto in = weight(\"shortconv.in_proj.weight\");","                 const auto conv = weight(\"shortconv.conv.weight\");","                 const auto out = weight(\"shortconv.out_proj.weight\");","+                OPENVINO_ASSERT(conv.ne(0) == *kernel,","+                                \"[GGUF] short-convolution weight width does not match shortconv.l_cache in layer \",","+                                layer);","                 if (lfm3)","                     OPENVINO_ASSERT(in.ne(0) == dims.embedding && in.ne(1) == int64_t{3} * dims.embedding &&","                                         conv.ne(0) == *kernel && conv.ne(1) == dims.embedding &&","@@ -109,7 +143,9 @@ class LfmBuilder : public ModelBuilder {","                                                         g.node(\"GGML_OP_MUL_MAT\", {in, cur}),","                                                         conv,","                                                         dims.embedding,","-                                                        \"conv_state_l\" + std::to_string(layer));","+                                                        \"conv_state_l\" + std::to_string(layer),","+                                                        true,","+                                                        conv_padding);","                 cur = g.node(\"GGML_OP_MUL_MAT\", {out, gated});","             } else {","                 if (lfm3) {","@@ -138,7 +174,11 @@ class LfmBuilder : public ModelBuilder {","         cur = g.build_norm(cur,","                            weights.require(lfm3 ? \"output_norm.weight\" : \"token_embd_norm.weight\"),","                            dims.norm_epsilon);","-        if (lfm3)","+        if (encoder) {","+            g.set_output(encoder_output(cur, output_weight, parameters.pooling_type), \"embeddings\");","+            return g.finish();","+        }","+        if (lfm3 && causal)","             g.set_output(cur, \"audio_hidden_states\");","         auto output = g.node(\"GGML_OP_MUL_MAT\", {output_weight, cur});","         if (detokenizer) {","@@ -150,6 +190,32 @@ class LfmBuilder : public ModelBuilder {","     }"," "," private:","+    // Pools [1, 1, T, D] like llama.cpp build_pooling, then applies the optional dense_2 projection.","+    GgufValue encoder_output(GgufValue cur, const GgufValue& dense, int pooling) {","+        const auto tokens = [&](int64_t start) {","+            return g.node(\"GGML_OP_VIEW\", {cur}, 3, {{\"view_slice\", std::vector<int64_t>{2, start, 1}}});","+        };","+        if (pooling == 1)","+            cur = g.node(\"GGML_OP_TRANSPOSE\", {g.node(\"GGML_OP_MEAN\", {g.node(\"GGML_OP_TRANSPOSE\", {cur})})});","+        else if (pooling == 2)","+            cur = tokens(0);","+        else if (pooling == 3)","+            cur = tokens(-1);","+        auto width = cur.ne(0);","+        if (dense) {","+            width = dense.ne(1);","+            OPENVINO_ASSERT(","+                dense.ne(0) == cur.ne(0) && g.metadata().get_int(\"lfm2.embedding_length_out\").value_or(width) == width,","+                \"[GGUF] LFM2 dense_2 must project the hidden size to embedding_length_out\");","+            cur = g.node(\"GGML_OP_MUL_MAT\", {dense, cur});","+            if (auto bias = g.tensors()(\"dense_2.bias\")) {","+                OPENVINO_ASSERT(bias.ne(0) == width, \"[GGUF] LFM2 dense_2.bias must match embedding_length_out\");","+                cur = g.node(\"GGML_OP_ADD\", {cur, bias});","+            }","+        }","+        return g.node(\"GGML_OP_RESHAPE\", {cur}, 0, {{\"reshape_target\", std::vector<int64_t>{-1, width}}});","+    }","+","     GgufGraphContext g;"," };"," }  // namespace","@@ -159,7 +225,8 @@ GgufValue build_lfm_short_conv(GgufGraphContext& g,","                                const GgufValue& conv_weight,","                                int64_t channels,","                                const std::string& state_name,","-                               bool batch_major) {","+                               bool batch_major,","+                               LfmConvPadding padding) {","     const auto slice = [&](const GgufValue& value, int64_t start, int64_t length) {","         return g.node(\"GGML_OP_VIEW\", {value}, 3, {{\"view_slice\", std::vector<int64_t>{3, start, length}}});","     };","@@ -167,9 +234,26 @@ GgufValue build_lfm_short_conv(GgufGraphContext& g,","     const auto bx =","         g.node(\"GGML_OP_TRANSPOSE\",","                {g.node(\"GGML_OP_MUL\", {slice(projected, 0, channels), slice(projected, 2 * channels, channels)})});","-    const auto state = g.add_input(state_name, ov::element::f32, {1, 1, channels, taps});","-    const auto window = g.node(\"GGML_OP_CONCAT\", {state, bx}, 0, {{\"concat_axis\", 0}});","-    g.add_recurrent_state(state, slice(window, -taps, taps));","+    const auto zeros = [&](const std::string& suffix, int64_t length) {","+        ov::Tensor value(ov::element::f32, {1, 1, static_cast<size_t>(channels), static_cast<size_t>(length)});","+        std::fill_n(value.data<float>(), value.get_size(), 0.0f);","+        return g.add_constant(state_name + suffix, value);","+    };","+    const auto concat = [&](const GgufValue& left, const GgufValue& right) {","+        return g.node(\"GGML_OP_CONCAT\", {left, right}, 0, {{\"concat_axis\", 0}});","+    };","+    GgufValue window;","+    if (padding == LfmConvPadding::STATE) {","+        const auto state = g.add_input(state_name, ov::element::f32, {1, 1, channels, taps});","+        window = concat(state, bx);","+        g.add_recurrent_state(state, slice(window, -taps, taps));","+    } else if (padding == LfmConvPadding::CAUSAL) {","+        window = concat(zeros(\".pad\", taps), bx);","+    } else {","+        OPENVINO_ASSERT(taps % 2 == 0, \"[GGUF] a centered short convolution requires an odd kernel\");","+        const auto pad = zeros(\".pad\", taps / 2);","+        window = concat(concat(pad, bx), pad);","+    }","     const auto conv = g.node(\"GGML_OP_SSM_CONV\", {window, conv_weight}, 0, {{\"batch_major\", batch_major}});","     return g.node(\"GGML_OP_MUL\", {slice(projected, channels, channels), conv});"," }"],"additions":102,"deletions":18,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/frontends/gguf/src/builder/arch/lfm_builder.hpp","lines":["@@ -13,11 +13,16 @@ namespace ov::frontend::gguf {"," std::shared_ptr<ModelBuilder> make_lfm_builder(const BuildContext& context);"," std::shared_ptr<Model